Filling in the Reason Code field is very important for the Wine Suite applications.
The standard **Reason Codes** table is extended by the **EOS WINE** app (EX080) with operational parameters for wine treatments, and by the **EOS WINE SIAN** app (EX083) with parameters used for ICQRF/SIAN electronic traceability.

### 1. Fields added by the EOS WINE (EX080)

| Field | Type | Functional use |
|---|---|
| Wine Treatment | Enables the reason code to be used in Wine Treatments. It acts as a filter: when creating and linking a treatment, only reason codes with this flag enabled can be selected. It is also the condition that makes the other Wine fields visible on the Reason Codes page. |
| Wine Treatment Multi Output | ndicates that the wine treatment generates multiple output products from the same source batch. When enabled, the treatment is created as a "Family" type order with a multi-output page. When disabled, a single-output treatment is created. |
| Wine Treatment No. Series | Specific number series assigned to wine treatments created using this reason code. It overrides the default number series defined in the Wine Setup. |
| Wine Treatment Routing No. | Production routing (certified routings only) proposed for treatments created with this reason code. It overrides the default routing defined in the Wine Setup. |
<br>

**Operational use:** Selecting the reason code in the New Wine Treatment page causes the system to automatically populate the number series and production routing, and determines whether to open the standard treatment page or the multi-output page.


### 2. Fields added by EOS WINE SIAN (EX083)

| Field | Functional Use |
|---|---|
| SIAN Operation Type Load | SIAN operation type (e.g., ARMC, IMBO, TAGL, SVIN, etc.) associated with load (positive) movements. When a positive movement is posted, it determines the operation used to update the SIAN register. |
| SIAN Operation Type Unload | Similar to the above, but for unload (negative) movements. It is also used as a filter in the operation product number lookups on treatment outputs/components. |
| SIAN Expiration Date Load | Expiration formula applied to the load operation. It calculates the expiration date of the SIAN register entry based on the posting date. |
| SIAN Expiration Date Unload | DateFormula. Same as above, but for the unload operation. |
| SIAN Enological Practice | Default enological practice (SIAN "Enological Practices" table). For receipt treatments/outputs (other than IMBO), it is propagated to the produced lot together with the practices inherited from the components, unless automation is disabled in the SIAN Setup. |
| Exemption Derogation | Exemption derogation code (SIAN "Derogation Obligation" table) reported in the SIAN register operation generated by the movement. |
| SIAN Skip Category Check | If enabled, skips the validation of allowed categories for the operation during transmission to the SIAN web service. |
| SIAN Expiration Date | Generic expiration field available on the Reason Codes page. In the current logic, the actual expiration date is managed by the dedicated Load/Unload expiration fields; therefore, this field acts as a residual/reference parameter. |
<br>

**Convention Note (SIAN):** the category check looks for a reason code whose code matches the operation name (e.g., reason code **"IMBO"**). On that reason code, the **"SIAN Category Check"** flag disables the validation. It is considered best practice to align reason code codes with the corresponding managed SIAN operation codes.

The **SIAN Operation Type Load** and the **SIAN Operation Type Unload** are identical for all wine treatment reason codes and for the bottling reason code (**IMBO**). The exceptions are the **CASD** (Purchase) and **USSD** (Sale) reason codes, where **CASD** must be set as the **SIAN Operation Type Load** and **USSD** as the **SIAN Operation Type Unload** (on both reason codes).

### 3. Setup Guidelines

- Enable **"Wine App Enabled"** in the **Wine Setup** to make the Wine/SIAN fields available and operational on reason codes.
- For each type of wine treatment, create a reason code with **"Wine Treatment" = Yes** and configure, where required, the number series, production routing, and multi-output flag.
- For SIAN traceability, configure at least the operation types (**Receipt/Shipment**) and, where applicable, the enological practice, exemption/derogation code, and expiration formulas.
- Pre-populate the SIAN **"Enological Practices"** and **"Derogation Obligation"** tables.